{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The dispute is confined to one line, and identifying it correctly matters. EV-FARE-00710 shows charged_total of SGD 31.00 against quoted_fare_sgd of SGD 25.00, and the four non-ERP lines on that ledger (base 3.80 + distance 14.15 + time 6.25 + platform fee 0.80) sum to exactly 25.00. The entire contested SGD 6.00 is therefore the single ERP pass-through line, and the only questions the tribunal has to decide are the pass-through questions under POL-RD-09 and the POL-RD-11(a) and (b) remedies - not a distance or time question.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00710", "EV-TRIP-00710"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.charged_total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider does not rest this dispute on a distance or time refund, and the policy closes that route on this record. The governing trace figure on EV-GPS-00710 is trace_distance_km 11.99 against a matched-itinerary optimal of 12.2 km, an excess of -0.21 km that fails both POL-RD-01 establishment tests, and the derived block records the status as 'no deviation'. Because the trip is RYDE_POOL, POL-RD-12 fixes the baseline as the matched-itinerary figure of 12.2 km and not the solo optimal of 8.5 km carried on EV-TRIP-00710, so the 3.7 km pooling difference cannot be claimed as excess either. What survives for the rider on an upfront-quoted trip is the pass-through limb that POL-RD-11(b) expressly preserves.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00710", "EV-TRIP-00710", "EV-FARE-00710"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-12", "POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's account of the booking terms is the only account of them anywhere in the bundle. At 07:28:40, while the trip was still running, the rider sent EV-CHAT-00710 MSG-00710-001 asking why all six dollars were on her booking when the booking said the ERP was shared, and the driver's only answer, MSG-00710-002 at 07:29:05, was 'Pay the full ERP on this booking' - a demand that neither contradicts the sharing term the rider names nor points to any clause or record placing the whole line on this rider. No booking-terms artifact is in the bundle. Under POL-RD-08 an assertion that identifies no artifact and no clause carries no weight, and under POL-RD-11(a) a pass-through line is deductible only to the extent it is properly chargeable.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00710", "EV-FARE-00710"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-11"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The gantry match that makes the line chargeable is carried only by the document that bills it. POL-RD-09(4) matches a gantry to the trace by comparing erp_gantry.lat and erp_gantry.lng against the trace, but those coordinates sit on EV-FARE-00710 - the same ledger that charges the SGD 6.00 - and the on_optimal_route flag is carried on that ledger too. The trace proximity reported on EV-GPS-00710 is a nearest fix at 0.0 m distance at the ledger's own charged_at instant of 07:30:40. Nothing independent in the bundle - no gantry registry, no receipt, no advisory - corroborates that this line belongs to this rider's booking.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00710", "EV-GPS-00710"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.erp_gantry_proximity.lines[0].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trip was a pooled one sharing its route with a second booking, which is exactly the factual setting the rider describes. EV-TRIP-00710 records vehicle_type RYDE_POOL with a matched-itinerary optimal of 12.2 km against a solo optimal of 8.5 km, so 3.7 km of the driven route exists to serve the co-rider that POL-RD-12 contemplates, and the rider said so in the chat at the time. Yet EV-FARE-00710 carries the ERP as one undivided SGD 6.00 line against this rider's booking with no allocation data anywhere in the bundle. On that state of the record the tribunal cannot hold that the whole line has been shown to be properly chargeable to this rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00710", "EV-FARE-00710", "EV-CHAT-00710"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-12", "POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "If the tribunal regards the allocation as undecidable on this record, the rider's fallback submission is ESCALATE under POL-RD-10 rather than NO_ACTION, because POL-RD-10 is terminal and holds the disputed amount rather than collecting it. That reading is supported by EV-FARE-00710's own note, which states that the POL-RD-09(4) gantry match radius is not a structured field and that 'the ERP figures report amounts and distances and decide no match' - the platform's ledger thus declines to decide the very match on which the charge against this rider survives.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00710", "EV-GPS-00710"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10", "POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.not_structured",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider: I have considered your point that the pool booking said the ERP was shared and that another rider was aboard. The contested SGD 6.00 is the only ERP line on the bill. Your trip was an upfront quote of SGD 25.00 (base SGD 3.80 + distance SGD 14.15 + time SGD 6.25 + platform fee SGD 0.80 = SGD 25.00 exactly), and the charged total was SGD 31.00, the extra being the SGD 6.00 ERP pass-through. Under POL-RD-11 an upfront-quoted, quoted_fare 25.00 trip gives no distance-or-time refund, so the only question is whether the SGD 6.00 ERP line is properly chargeable. It is. The single gantry ('Matched itinerary gantry') lies on the matched-itinerary optimal route, and the GPS trace passes it: the nearest fix is 0.0 m from the gantry coordinates at 07:30:40, inside the 250 m match radius POL-RD-09(4) applies. That makes it a crossed, on-route gantry, not a phantom line, so no billing-integrity refund arises and the POL-RD-11(a) arithmetic is charged_total 31.00 - quoted_fare 25.00 - properly chargeable ERP 6.00 = 0.00. Your argument that the gantry coordinates sit only on the ledger that bills them does not change this: POL-RD-09(4) prescribes exactly that comparison, and the trace independently places a fix at the gantry at the charged instant. Your request for a pro-rata share fails for a separate reason - the policy contains no mechanism to split a metered ERP pass-through between co-riders. POL-RD-12 (pooled trips) adjusts only the distance baseline and does not touch ERP, and no booking-terms artifact showing a shared-ERP term exists in the bundle; the only source for that term is your own message. I also cannot find a distance deviation: the governing trace figure is 11.99 km against the matched-itinerary optimal of 12.2 km, an excess of -0.21 km (-1.72%), which fails both POL-RD-01 tests, and the 8.5 km solo optimal is not the baseline for a RYDE_POOL trip. Your fallback request for ESCALATE is declined: no POL-RD-10 trigger fires (see below). To the driver: the ERP line stands as charged, and your statement that the gantry was crossed on the matched itinerary is corroborated by the trace. Your chat message 'Pay the full ERP on this booking' does not affect the outcome - the line is chargeable because the trace crossed an on-route gantry, not because you demanded payment. No POL-RD-04 rider-requested detour is in play (the chat contains no instruction, and no waypoint), and no POL-RD-06 conduct referral arises: there is no material deviation and no repeat pattern (deviation_flags_90d 0 over completed_trips_90d 250). On escalation, POL-RD-10 is not engaged: the trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c) (100% coverage, no gaps, 10 s sampling), the trip identifiers and timestamps agree across the trip record, trace and ledger, no refund computation exceeds any ceiling, and the ERP line has its counterpart in the trace. The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00710-01, weight 0.0) is neutral, since neither party asserted an external traffic cause; and the ledger's note that the gantry match radius is not a structured field is a data-modelling note, not a finding that the match is undecidable - POL-RD-09(4) supplies the test and the record satisfies it. Result: the charge stands. payment_status remains CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd remains 0.00. Confidence 0.90, capped by the weight-1.0 artifacts that carry the deciding fact (the GPS trace and the fare breakdown).",
    "referrals": []
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
